  "$Comment": "The in-game screen for the track world rules, on the owner menu (/zigadmin): one row per rule in force, each opening its switch, what gains there and what the picks grant there, every setting saved straight into mods/ziggfreedcommon/track-world-rules.json under that rule's id, beside the value it has without your file. Above the rows, one switch turns every rule off at once: it writes the file's own $Enabled at the top of the file, the one $ key this screen may write. The line at the top counts the problems the track audit finds in the rules. Which worlds a rule covers and every new rule stay in the files. Every word is a key of ziggfreedcommon.track.lang. Retune this screen (its place on the menu, a bound) in mods/ziggfreedcommon/owner-forms.json under the id Track_World_Rules.",
